          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Monadic descent
            is a way to encode
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered categories
            (equivalently, via the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctors"} pseudofunctors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibrations
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebraic tools
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monads
            and related structures from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to B
            comes naturally equipped not only with a notion of pullback, but also of pushforward. Combined these provide pull-push-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monads
            that may be used to encode the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            property of the fibration.
          %p
            A morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : b_1 \to b_2
            in the base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\dashv U
            where
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ≕
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↔
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F
                  \\;\colon\;
                  E_{b_1}
                  \\eqqcolon
                  A
                  \\leftrightarrow
                  B
                  \\coloneqq
                  E_{b_2}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  U
                  \\mathrlap{\,,}
          %p
            and we ask whether
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functor
          %p
            This is the original description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            with values in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
          %p
            The archetypical and motivating example is that of the bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ring
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod \to Ring
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rings"} Rings
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{(-)}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            over it. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f_! \dashv f^\ast \dashv f_\ast)
                  \\colon
                  \\mathcal{C}_X
                  \\stackrel{\overset{f_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{f_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  \\mathcal{C}_Y
          %p
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi f
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi J
                    %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (T_f \dashv J_f) \coloneqq (f^\ast f_! \dashv f^\ast f_\ast)
          %p
            for the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            There is a standard definition of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Desc
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Desc_{\mathcal{C}}(f)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+data"} descent data
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{(-)}
            along
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Y
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Desc
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C}_{Y} \longrightarrow Desc_{\mathcal{C}}(f)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is called (with respect to the given bifibration
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{(-)}
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %em descent morphism
                if this comparison map is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %li
              %p
                an
                %em effective descent morphism
                if the comparison map is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p
            Now the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9nabou%E2%80%93Roubaud+theorem"} Bénabou–Roubaud theorem
            states that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{(-)}
            satisfies the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck%E2%80%93Chevalley+condition"} Beck–Chevalley condition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebra over a monad
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_f
            (equivalently a coalgebra for
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_f
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93Moore+category"} Eilenberg–Moore category
            for these (co-)monads
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Desc
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi EM
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Desc_{\mathcal{C}}(f)
                  \\simeq
                  EM(T_f)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{(-)}
            satisfies the BC condition, then a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %em is effective descent
            precisely if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \colon \mathcal{C}_{Y} \to \mathcal{C}_{X}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic"} monadic
            %em is descent
            precisely if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            is of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+type"} descent type
          %p This is the monadic formulation of descent theory, “monadic descent”.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#JanelidzeTholen94"} Janelidze–Tholen 94, pp. 247-248 (3-4 of 37)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The main theorem is Beck’s
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
          %p
            Given a Grothendieck
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:E\to B
            and a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:b\to b'
            in the base category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!:E_b\to E_{b'}
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:E_{b'}\to E_b
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!\dashv f^*
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9nabou%E2%80%93Roubaud+theorem"} Bénabou–Roubaud theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+descent+morphism"} effective descent morphism
            (with respect to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            induced by the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!\dashv f^*
            is monadic.
          %p
            We should now see that some instances of categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            data are canonically equivalent to and can be reexpressed via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93Moore+category"} Eilenberg–Moore categories
            of monads, or dually comonads.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#DescentForTheCodomainFibration Descent for the codomain fibration
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Cartesian+closed+category"} locally Cartesian closed category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
            (e.g. a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            are precisely the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphisms"} regular epimorphisms
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#JanelidzeTholen94"} Janelidze–Tholen 94, 2.4
          %p
            Hence for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
            any morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f_! \dashv f^\ast \dashv f_\ast) \colon \mathcal{C}_{/X} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}_{/Y}
          %p
            the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/Y}
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93Moore+category"} Eilenberg–Moore category
            of algebras over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast f_!
            (equivalently: of coalgebras of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast f_\ast
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
          %p
            (Use
            %a{:href => "conservative+functor#PullbackAlongEpimorphisms"} conservative pullback along epimorphisms
            in the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
          %h3#ForCodomainFibs Monadic descent of bundles
          %p
            One of the most basic examples of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cod
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod : [I,C] \to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [I,C]
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod
            sends any arrow in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
          %p
            An object in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in C
            is a morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            of bundles.
          %p
            Other examples of monadic descent often find a useful interpretation when relating them back to monadic descent for codomain fibrations. For instance (co)monadic descent for
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
          %p
            We show in the following that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cod
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod : [I,C] \to C
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : Y\to X
            a morphism in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [I,C]_Y
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* f_*
            encodes and is encoded by a “geometric”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            datum: that it is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Y
            %li
              %p
                equipped with a transition function between its two pullbacks to double
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \times_X Y
            %li
              %p
                which satisfies on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \times_X Y \times_X Y
                the usual cocycle condition.
          %h4#motivation_failure_of_pushforward_for_principal_bundles Motivation: failure of push-forward for principal bundles
          %p
            Monadic methods can be applied to the study of descent of structures that cannot only be pulled back, such as
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            (a topological one, say, i.e. a morphism in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is simply the composite map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X \to Z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Z
            living over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
          %p
            While that always exists as such, it will in general not be a principal bundle anymore: the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Z
            over points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in Z
            consist of many copies of the fibers of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            over points in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            So principal bundles do have a canonical notion of push-forward, but it leads outside the category of principal bundles and lands generally in some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
          %p
            On the other hand, as we will see in detail below, if we take a principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            and
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                first push it forward in this generalized sense to an object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Z
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top/Z
            %li
              %p
                and
                %strong then
                pull back the result of that again along
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Z
                the result, while still not a principal bundle, is the total space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                of the bundle pulled back to the first term in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Z
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
                property of the bundle.
          %p But the composite operation of pushforward of overcategories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi push
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  push(f) : Top/X \to Top/Z
          %p followed by pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pull
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  pull(f) : Top/Z \to Top/X
          %p
            is nothing but the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            associated to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Z
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain bifibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cod
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod : [I,Top] \to Top
          %p
            So by regarding principal bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            more generally as just objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top/X
            we make the tools of monadic descent applicable to them.
          %h4#the_monad The monad
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cod
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  cod : [I,C] \to C
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            (as described there, in detail). Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            over an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
          %p
            The direct image operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi push
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} push(f)
            associated to a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : Y \to X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi push
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  push(\pi) : C/Y \to  C/X
          %p
            obtained by postcomposition with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P \to Y) \in C/Y
            to the composite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi π
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Y \stackrel{\pi}{\to} X
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
          %p
            The inverse image operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pull
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pull(f)
            associated to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ←
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi pull
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C/Y \leftarrow C/X : pull(\pi)
          %p
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            along
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Q \to X) \in C/X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \times_X Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/Y
            in terms of the canonical projection morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \times_X Y\to Y
            out of the pullback.
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi π
                  %mo =
                  %mi pull
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi push
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T_\pi = pull(\pi) \circ push(\pi) : C/Y \to C/Y
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            built from these two
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
          %h4#the_algebras_over_the_monad_geometric_descent_data The algebras over the monad: geometric descent data
          %p
            We spell out in detail the data of an algebra over the above monad, and show that this encodes precisely the familiar geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            datum for a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
          %p
            To that end, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P, \rho)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi P
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ⇓
                            %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi T
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi P
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P : {*} \to C/Y
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; C/Y
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{P}}
                  \\nearrow  &amp;\Downarrow^{\rho}&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{T}}
                  \\\
                  {*} &amp;&amp;\stackrel{P}{\to}&amp;&amp; C/Y
                  }
          %p
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} algebra over
            our monad. In components this is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            equipped with a morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_P : T P \to P
          %p
            The object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T P \in [I,C]_Y
            is given by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                first pushing
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Y
                forward along
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : Y \to X
                to the object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Y \to X
            %li
              %p
                then pulling this back along
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                to yield the left vertical morphism in
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                              %mi P
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi P
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi π
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi π
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Y \times_X P &amp;\to&amp; P
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; Y
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}}
                      \\\
                      Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; X
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                This
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                along a composite of morphisms may be computed as two consecutive pullbacks. The first one is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                              %mi Y
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi π
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi π
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Y \times_X Y &amp;\to&amp; Y
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}}
                      \\\
                      Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; X
                      }
              %p
                which is the first term in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                to
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\times_X Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Y
                              %mi P
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi P
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                              %mi Y
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi π
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi π
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      (Y \times_X Y) \times_Y P &amp;\to&amp; P
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      Y \times_X Y &amp;\to&amp; Y
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}}
                      \\\
                      Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; X
                      }
                      \\,.
          %p
            Therefore the action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_T : T P \to P
            of our
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is given in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (Y \times_X Y) \times_Y P &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\rho}{\to}&amp;&amp;
                  P
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; Y
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            As an example, think of this in the context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Top
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi  \colon Y \to X
            coming from an open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \coprod_i U_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo =
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P = Y \times G
            a trivial
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi Y
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \times_X Y = \coprod_{i j} U_i \cap U_j
            is the union of double intersection of covering patches, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %mi P
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y \times_X Y) \times_Y P = (\coprod_{i j} U_i \cap U_j \times G)
            is to be thought of as the trivial
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            acts as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \coprod_{i j} : (U_i \cap U_j \times G) \to \coprod_i U_i \times G
          %p
            and thus maps the trivial
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_j
            on the intersection with the trivial
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            = succeed "." do
              %em transition function
            = succeed "-equivariant," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            datum for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          %h3#AlongPrincipalBundle
            Monadic descent
            %em along
            principal bundles
          %h4#idea_2 Idea
          %p
            In the
            %a{:href => "#ForCodomainFibs"} above section
            we considered monadic descent
            %em of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Y
            %em along
            morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
          %p
            Now we consider monadic descent
            %em along
            morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : P \to X
            that happen to be
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            this describes the situation where we ask for a bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \to P
            that sits over the total space of another (principal) bundle to descend down along that bundle map to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h4#setup Setup
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be an internal group in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu: P\times G\to P
            be a right principal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:P\times G\to P
            the projection. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi:P\to X
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principality condition
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\times G \to P\times_X P
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi pg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,g)\mapsto (p,pg)
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi p
                    %mi ν
                  %mi P
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi π
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P\times G \overset{\nu}\underset{p}\rightrightarrows P \overset{\pi}\to X
          %p
            We do not assume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            to be trivial. We have also the two projections
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi P
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                  %mi P
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi π
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P\times_X P \overset{p_1}\underset{p_2}\rightrightarrows P \overset{\pi}\to X
          %p
            out of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1,p_2
            make a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu,p
            make also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            of its own
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
          %h4#the_two_different_monads The two different monads
          %p
            We now describe the monadic descent along the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : P \to X
            from above for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cod
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod : [I,C] \to C
          %p
            There are two monads acting on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/P
            whose underlying functors are
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi π
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T := \pi^* \pi_!
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo !
                      %msup
                        %mi ν
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde T := p_! \nu^*
          %p
            The first monad,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the usual one for monadic descent along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            induced from a pair of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
          %p
            The second one,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            and is defined as follows:
          %p
            to construct the component
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_h
            of the transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu: p_! \nu^* p_!\nu^*\to p_!\nu^*
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h: L\to P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu^* p_! \nu^* h
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! \nu^* h
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ν
                            %mo *
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mo !
                          %msup
                            %mi ν
                            %mo *
                          %mi L
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi h
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ν
                            %mo *
                          %mi L
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi L
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %munder
                              %mi ν
                              %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\nu^* p_! \nu^* L
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\mu_h}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;\nu^* L &amp;\to&amp; L
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  P &amp;\stackrel{\stackrel{p}{\to}}{\underset{\to}{\nu}}&amp;
                  X
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            which can be interpreted as a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!\nu^* p_! \nu^* h\to p_* \nu^* h
            because the domains of the maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!\nu^* p_! \nu^* h
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu^* p_! \nu^* h
            are the same by the definition and the commuting triangles can be checked easily.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi P
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\times G \cong P\times_X P
            now induces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo !
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! \nu^* h \cong \pi^* \pi_! h
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:L\to P
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mo !
                          %msup
                            %mi ν
                            %mo *
                          %mi L
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mo *
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mo !
                          %mi L
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi L
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi h
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mo ×
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi π
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  p_! \nu^* L &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; \pi^* \pi_! L &amp;\to&amp; L
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{h}}
                  \\\
                  P \times G &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; P \times_X P &amp;\to&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; P &amp;\to&amp; X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p This rule extends to an isomorphism of monads
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ≃
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T \simeq \tilde T
                  \\,.
          %p
            As a corollary, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93Moore+category"} Eilenberg–Moore categories
            of the two monads are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! \nu^*
            are certain maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi ν
                      %mo *
                    %mi h
                    %mo →
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!\nu^*h\to h
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu^* h\to p^* h
            by adjointness. This matches one of the definitions for an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+sheaf"} equivariant sheaf
          %p
            The map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : P\to X
            of the principal bundle is an
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+descent+morphism"} effective descent morphism
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            if the comparison functor for any of the two above isomorphic monads above is an equivalence of categories.
          %h3#monadic_descent_of_modules Monadic descent of modules
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi Rings
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod \to Rings
            from the category of modules over any ring, mapping each module to the ring that it is a module over. This models, dually, an algebraic version of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
          %p
            Comonadic descent for this bifibration (equivalently monadic descent for its formal dual,
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Rings
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod^{op} \to Rings^{op}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
          %h3#gluing_categories_from_localizations Gluing categories from localizations
          %p
            Another example is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/zoranskoda/show/gluing+categories+from+localizations"} gluing categories from localizations
          %h2#higher_category_theoretical_version Higher category theoretical version
          %p
            All the ingredients of monadic descent generalize from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+monadic+descent"} higher monadic descent
            that relates to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+monadic+descent"}> higher monadic descent
              \.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+geometric+morphism"} surjective geometric morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomological+descent"} cohomological descent
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+morphism"} descent morphism
                %li
                  %p
                    %strong monadic descent
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley condition
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+monadic+descent"} higher monadic descent
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+in+noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} descent in noncommutative algebraic geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"}> sheaf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaf"} (2,1)-sheaf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"} 2-sheaf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9nabou%E2%80%93Roubaud+theorem"} Bénabou–Roubaud theorem
            on monadic descent is due to:
          %ul
            %li#BenabouRoubaud70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Roubaud"} Jacques Roubaud
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monades et descente
              %strong 270
              (1970) 96-98 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k480298g/f100"}> gallica:12148/bpt6k480298g/f100
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BenabouRoubaud-MonadesEtDescente.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Heinig"} Peter Heinig
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/279152"} MO:q/279152
          %p Review and further developments:
          %ul
            %li#JanelidzeTholen94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Janelidze"}> George Janelidze
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Facets of descent I
                %strong 2
                3 (1994) 245-281 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00878100"}> doi:10.1007/BF00878100
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#JanelidzeTholen97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Janelidze"}> George Janelidze
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Facets of descent II
                %strong 5
                3 (1997) 229-248 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1008697013769"}> doi:10.1023/A:1008697013769
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Janelidze"}> George Janelidze
                , Manuela Sobral,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Beyond Barr exactness: effective descent morphisms
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                (ed.)
                %em Categ. Foundations
                Enc. Math. Appl. (2003)
            %li
              %p
                Bachuki Mesablishvili,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monads of effective descent type and comonadicity
                = succeed ":1" do
                  %strong 16
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/16/1/16-01abs.html"} link
            %li
              %ul
                %li
                  Bachuki Mesablishvili:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Pure morphisms of commutative rings are effective descent morphisms for modules—a new proof
                  %strong 7
                  3 (2000) 38–42
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Stefan Caenepeel,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Janelidze"} George Janelidze
                %em Monadic approach to Galois descent and cohomology
                \&amp;lbrack
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.1674"}> arXiv:0812.1674
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                S. Caenepeel:
                %em Galois corings from the descent theory point of view,
                in: Fields Inst. Commun.
                %strong 43
                (2004) 163–186
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomasz+Brzezi%C5%84ski"}> Tomasz Brzeziński
                , Adrian Vazquez Marquez, Joost Vercruysse,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Eilenberg–Moore category and a Beck-type theorem for a Morita context
                %strong 19
                (2011) 821 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-009-9217-0"}> doi:10.1007/s10485-009-9217-0
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p An expository overview:
          %ul
            %li
              Rui Prezado,chapter 2 of:
              %em Some aspects of descent theory and applications
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.09337"}> arXiv:2502.09337
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Balmer"}> Paul Balmer
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Descent in triangulated categories
              %strong 353
              1 (2012) 109–125
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-monads"} (infinity,1)-monads
          %ul
            %li#Hess10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
              , section 2 of:
              %em A general framework for homotopic descent and codescent
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.1556"}> arXiv:1001.1556
              \&amp;rbrack;
